-- The interleaved wand (w3-b): [DP, Triple, SB, DP, SB, SB] — the general binding, first spelling: gamma over an order-derived srel. Twin of 123-modifier-chain.bqn (the interleaved section). (was w3-modifier-chain-b)
-- The interleaved wand breaks the shortcut: each modifier binds to ITS next projectile. The binding is a relation derived from slot geometry, and the damage write is the grouped fold over it.
-- binds' groups each projectile with the modifiers whose next projectile is that slot, the BQN twin's inverted NextP. The grouped fold sends DP0 through Triple to its first bolt and DP3 to the next; the single-target shortcut fails on this fixture.
--! registry ../registries/124-modifier-chain-b.reg
--! expect bal = 0 1 3 2 2 1 0
--! expect minBal = 0 1 1 1 1 1 0
--! expect member = 0 1 1 1 1 1 1
--! expect damage = 0 0 0 13 0 13 3

Spell , Bal = 1 + (+\ (DrawAdd - 1) @ Spell)
Spell , MinBal = 0 - (max\ (0 - Bal) @ Spell)
Spell @ deck & (Slot == 0 | prev.MinBal > 0) , +Member
Spell & Proj & Member , Damage += 10 * (#/ (binds' & (Mod & Member)))
